{
  "about": [
    "Every field the engine worker may write into result.json, by object, and what the core's",
    "strict types accept for it. Checked from both sides: crates/hotend-core/tests/",
    "engine_result_contract.rs holds the Rust types to this list (no field more, none less),",
    "and python/tests/result_contract.py holds every result of the worker's tests to it. See",
    "docs/PROTOCOL.md section 3.3, 'How a result is validated'.",
    "Types: text, path, name, piece, question_id, check_id, short_id, color, view, number,",
    "integer, count (0 or more), bool, object (opaque JSON object), any (opaque JSON),",
    "one_of:a,b, @object, [T], [T;n] (exactly n), {K:T}. '|null': may be null. A final '?':",
    "may be absent. core_only: part of the type, but the worker never writes it.",
    "max_items: the most entries of a list or map the core accepts. max_json_bytes: the longest",
    "compact JSON text of a field; max_result_bytes: of the whole file. other_bounds: lists and",
    "maps without a count of their own, and what bounds them. Free text has no maximum here: the",
    "core cuts it. JSON inside `any` and `object` is bounded by its field's max_json_bytes, or",
    "by the whole file alone (checks[].data, results, candidates, gauge args)."
  ],
  "ops": ["build", "measure", "export", "views", "docs", "prepare", "gauge", "calibrate", "sweep"],
  "ops_the_core_never_requests": ["references"],
  "objects": {
